{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790979784,"nonce":"VCFVfnCn9KBJjuaArXIz20b7s4c=","message":"Landed as `view: the feature tier is optional, expand states its rules, quickstart names the views (f9c991e)`, on the same branch as f4426ff.\n\n**(1) The tier is renamed, not the footnote patched.** `view.Feature` is `view.Optional`, printing `optional`, and the footnote reads \"An `optional` argument has no default: name it and the view does that thing, leave it out and it does not.\" Renaming was the honest fix: the tier was always \"optional with no default\", and `feature` plus that footnote read as a roadmap. The reason is recorded in the `Tier` doc comment, in `kindLong`'s comment, and in a paragraph of the design doc (Arguments, per kind). `view/view_test.go` now expects `group_by (optional)` in the unknown-argument error, and `commands/view/view_test.go` asserts the footnote says `has no default` and does *not* say `not drawn yet`.\n\n**(2) and (3) `expand`'s description** is one `expandDoc` shared by the list and the gantt, and it states the three things a reader cannot guess: either side of a relation is a name it takes (`parent` stored, `children` the inverse), a layer's `query` runs over that row's own unarchived children and not over the store, and a layer's `expand` is the level below. The shape is spelled out in the same line, so `--help` is now the whole contract. `group_by` says what `(none)` is, on all four kinds that take one.\n\n**The quickstart** gains a Views paragraph in \"Where everything else is\": the five kinds, that `git work view KIND KWARGS` takes one JSON object, that `git work view list --help` is the reference for `work.view.list(**kwargs)` too, what the three tiers mean, and a line each on `query`, `group_by` and `expand`. `commands/quickstart_test.go` still passes — the only command it names there is `git work view list --help`, which resolves.\n\n`doc/md/git-work_view_*.md` and `doc/man/git-work-view-*.1` were regenerated (`go run doc/generate.go`); they were stale from before the help's column widths changed, which is why the diff is bigger than the wording. Unrelated stale pages (issue, flow, the ungenerated jira/quickstart/sync/matrix pages) were left alone rather than swept into this change.\n\nDone together with f4426ff, as decided: the `expand` description describes the layer spec that issue introduced.","files":null}]}